{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["And the reason for <b>I begin to put your dread</b> — with respect to Israel, that all the peoples will fear them and the men of Canaan will go out to meet them with melting hearts, but HaShem hardened their spirit, saying: it is better for us to die by the sword than to become their slaves. For what reason is there to say concerning Moses, 'I begin to put your dread and fear upon the face of the peoples under all the heavens,' when he will wage war only against these two kings? Rather, it is a promise to Israel and to Joshua, as He said to him (Deuteronomy 3:21): 'Your eyes have seen,' etc. And this is the meaning of 'Begin to take possession of his land' (Deuteronomy 2:31)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:44:29.695220926Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}